(begin-tx "RDUI-03 -- the composer returns a whole object, and its fallback has a contract")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
;;==== RDUI-03 · 01 · namespace ==== ==============================================================
(print "--- [RDUI-03 · 01 · namespace] ---")
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
;;==== RDUI-03 · 02 · the composer, and what is NOT pinned here ==== ==============================
(print "--- [RDUI-03 · 02 · the composer, and what is NOT pinned here] ---")
;;WHAT IS PINNED: the composer returns all five members, each zone answers, and UDC_ZeroZone --
;;the value a failing zone yields -- carries zone-ok false, which is how a caller distinguishes a
;;DEAD zone from one whose numbers happen to be zero. The old all-or-nothing header could not
;;express that difference at all.
;;
;;WHAT IS NOT PINNED, stated plainly rather than faked: there is no assertion here that a LIVE
;;zone failure leaves the other four standing. Two attempts were made and both were wrong, which
;;is worth recording because each looked convincing:
;;
;;  1. A non-existent account. Does not fail -- DALOS reads through `with-default-read`, so a
;;     stranger returns zeroes and zone 1 reports zone-ok TRUE. The assertion passed as a
;;     failure-case while proving nothing.
;;  2. Loading without the SWP issuance suite, so zone 4 has no pools to price against. Also
;;     does not fail -- URC_OuroPrimordialPrice returns 0.0, and zone 1 rendered "<0.001¢".
;;
;;Both are the SAME property and it is a good one: Ouronet's sovereign readers default rather
;;than throw. It also means a zone failure cannot be contrived from fixture state, and the only
;;honest way to pin the degrade path is a module deployed against a deliberately absent
;;dependency -- a second boot, for a branch whose mechanism is three `try` forms. Not worth it
;;today; worth knowing the gap is deliberate and not an oversight.
;;NO MODULE-ADMIN GRANT, AND THAT IS THE POINT. An earlier draft of this block needed
;;(env-module-admin ouronet-ns.DALOS) because URC_01|Header reported the Ouronet account count
;;via a cross-module `keys` scan -- admin-gated by Pact, local-only on chain, and impossible to
;;put inside a `try`. _conformance.py's cross-module-scan rule refused it the moment a Pact
;;function CALLED the scan rather than inlining it, which is exactly the premise that rule
;;exists to keep honest.
;;
;;The field is gone and the header is better for it: no --allowReadsInLocal dependency, no admin
;;grant to call or to test, and every zone now degrades where z3-v1 could take the whole page
;;down. A UI wanting the number calls ouronet-ns.DALOS.URH_AccountCounter -- DALOS scanning its
;;OWN table, not admin-gated -- for one extra round trip.
(let
    (
        (h:object (O-UI-ONE.URC_01|Header KST.ANHD))
        (z:object (O-UI-ONE.UDC_ZeroZone))
    )
    (map print
        [
            (expect "<<RDUI-03>> the zero-zone fallback carries zone-ok FALSE -- the signal a \
                \ caller needs to tell a dead zone from a zero-valued one"
                false (at "zone-ok" z))
            ;;THE SHAPE IS THE CONTRACT. These four keys are what DPL-UR::URC_0001_HeaderV3
            ;;returned, so a consumer swaps the module path and changes nothing else. Asserting
            ;;the KEYS rather than the values is the point: values move every block, the shape
            ;;must not, and it is the shape an app breaks on.
            (expect "<<RDUI-03>> flat: zone 1 reports its Elite name in z1-t1"
                true (!= (at "z1-t1" h) "--"))
            (expect "<<RDUI-03>> flat: zone 2 reports an index name in z2-t1"
                (O-UI-ONE.UC_Index (ouronet-ns.ATS.URC_Index (at 0 (O-UI-ONE.URC_IndexIds))))
                (at "z2-v1" h))
            (expect "<<RDUI-03>> flat: zone 4 prices IGNIS at a flat cent"
                "1.000¢" (at "z4-v1" h))
            (expect "<<RDUI-03>> ...and resident-ignis is the fifth member, matching its own read"
                (O-UI-ONE.URC_ResidentIgnis KST.ANHD) (at "resident-ignis" h))
            ;;THE FOUR OK-FLAGS ARE THE THING THE OLD HEADER COULD NOT EXPRESS. One eager `let`
            ;;meant any single failure returned NOTHING; here a dead zone leaves its fields at
            ;;"--" and flags itself, and the other three still render.
            (expect "<<RDUI-03>> all four zones report ok on a healthy chain"
                [true true true true]
                [(at "z1-ok" h) (at "z2-ok" h) (at "z3-ok" h) (at "z4-ok" h)])
            ;;z3-v1 is the non-degradable field: it needs a `keys` scan, a scan cannot live in a
            ;;`try`, so its failure takes the whole header. That it answers at all here is only
            ;;because of the env-module-admin grant above.
            (expect "<<RDUI-03>> z3-v1 is a placeholder -- the cross-module account scan was \
                \ removed, which is what makes this whole block runnable without a module-admin \
                \ grant and every zone degradable"
                "--" (at "z3-v1" h))
        ]
    )
)
(commit-tx)

